{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794103993,"nonce":"d+FT2lXf9zBTBEsNt87bdp2f2jI=","title":"Key hints are drawn on the bottom line only","message":"## Design\n\n**Aspect changed:** `doc/design/tui.md`, \"The bottom line is two places\" (or a heading of its own, if it carries its own reasoning and citations).\n\n- **No box, picker, editor or widget draws key hints**: they are on the bottom line, as the search, flow and query boxes already have them (`withBox`, `tui/palette.go`). Two copies of one list drift, and do: the editor's footer says \"saves\" where the bottom line says \"write\".\n- Removed: `editor.View`'s footers (`tui/edit.go`, `enter saves · esc cancels` and kin) and `descFooter` (`tui/show.go`). The bottom line's wording wins where they disagree.\n- **The help (`?`) gets the bottom line too**, saying `esc close`. Its last line, `esc x is alt+x · esc ?: close`, goes: `esc` closes the help on its first press, so `esc ?` is never read, and the sentence explaining the table reads as a hint. The table gets column headers instead (keys, alt, palette, action).\n- The palette's letters are its content, not hints, and stay.\n- A test checks that the editor's, the box's and the help's views draw no hint text.\n- Lands before the $EDITOR story, which touches the same hints and `descFooter`.\n\nDesign approved by Luis on 2026-11-07, in a combined review of four stories (box column, side-table arrows, $EDITOR, hints on the bottom line).","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}